#
# Hefesto patch series for ngspice-47 (a80f6e3e), applied in this order with
# `patch -p1` by cmake/ApplyPatchSeries.cmake and by
# tools/golden/container/build_ngspice.sh. Each line is one patch file; the
# comment block above it is its justification (openspec/changes/m9-lvs-simulation
# design D9, tasks 5.1). The patch level of the version string
# `<release>-hefesto<n>` is `hefesto_level` in ../pin.json: raise it whenever
# this list or any patch changes. tools/ngspice_manifest.py copies these
# justifications into ngspice-manifest.json.
#
# Numerical behaviour: 0001 and 0002 change no result (they change where code
# is found, not what it computes). 0003 and 0004 change the random draws of
# every deck that uses agauss/aunif/sgauss/trnoise/trrandom with a given seed,
# relative to stock ngspice-47, on purpose: stock draws differ between C
# libraries and between processes. Decks without random functions are not
# affected.

# 0001 Static OSDI registry.
# Requirement "OSDI compact models" and "No runtime loading of executable
# code on iPadOS" (simulation-engine-embedding): `osdi`/`pre_osdi` resolve a
# built-in module by basename on every platform, so results never depend on
# .osdi files on the host, and other files load only while the ngspice
# variable `hefesto_osdi_static_only` is unset (the adapter sets it unless the
# user allows external OSDI models). Only osdiregistry.c's file lookup and
# symbol lookup change; the descriptor handling is untouched.
0001-static-osdi-registry.patch

# 0002 Static code-model registration.
# Feature table "XSPICE code models: compiled in statically": the analog,
# digital (without d_cosim), spice2poly and xtradev code models are compiled
# into libngspice-hefesto and registered when the device table is created,
# so no .cm file is ever dlopen'ed (no runtime loading on iPadOS; the same
# registry on every platform; works with ngSpice_nospinit()). The core
# functions the code models call are the same ones the dynamic coreInfo
# table points to (xspice/cm/cmexport.c).
0002-static-code-model-registration.patch

# 0003 Portable generator seeding.
# simulation-monte-carlo "Portable random numbers": the stock TausSeed() takes
# its state from rand(), whose sequence differs between glibc, macOS libc and
# the iPadOS libc, so the same seed gave different Monte Carlo samples per
# platform. The eight state words become 129 + (SplitMix64_k(seed) mod 32639);
# the generator itself is unchanged. The scenario "Generator state for seed 1"
# (29963, 3443, 21757, 5511, 10925, 11052, 26345, 26017) is checked by
# tests/test_portable_seed.py.
0003-portable-seeding.patch

# 0004 Deterministic initialisation.
# simulation-engine-embedding "Deterministic engine initialisation":
# - initw() seeded the Gaussian pool of trnoise/trrandom from getpid(), so two
#   engines differed even after the same `setseed`; it now restarts from the
#   last seed;
# - `setseed <n>` refills that pool, so a worker reused between jobs (design
#   D9) draws exactly as a fresh worker after the same `setseed`;
# - on hosts with pwd.h (Linux, macOS) ngSpice_Init read ./.spiceinit or
#   ~/.spiceinit even after ngSpice_nospiceinit(); the call is now honoured
#   there as it already was on the other branch;
# - ngSpice_nospinit()/ngSpice_nospiceinit(), which must be called before
#   ngSpice_Init(), dereferenced the not yet created simulator (if_option ->
#   ft_find_analysis) and crashed; if_option() now treats any variable as a
#   plain front-end variable while there is no simulator.
0004-deterministic-initialisation.patch
